From b175022ada460a887b1e8f23c9f5cf48461ac285 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 15:21:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32: silence spurious devlink error for SCMI
 crypto on stm32mp15
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

rng1/cryp1/hash1 are children of the ETZPC firewall bus and get their
clocks/resets from SCMI. The bus populates its children late, so
fw_devlink tries a proxy link from the bus to the SCMI device and logs:

  stm32-etzpc 5c007000.bus: Failed to create device link (0x180) with
  supplier scmi_dev.2 for /soc/bus@5c007000/rng@54003000

Mark the SCMI providers as post-init-providers so fw_devlink skips the
link. The devices still probe normally.

Change-Id: Iad76b00e1d18d1a41b17c68cc60315e873c8f0ba
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/576943
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
